{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And now.</b> If you now accept it upon yourselves, it will be pleasing to you from here onward, for all beginnings are hard (Mekhilta)." "<b>And you shall keep My covenant.</b> That I may make a covenant with you to keep the Torah." "<b>A treasure.</b> A cherished treasure, like ״וּסְגֻלַּת מְלָכִים״ (Ecclesiastes 2) — precious vessels and gemstones that kings store away. So too you shall be to Me a treasure beyond the other nations. And do not say: you alone are Mine and I have no others alongside you, so what do I have further that your cherishedness would be recognized?" "<b>For all the earth is Mine.</b> And they are in My eyes and before Me altogether."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:04.220964307Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}